within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.C_CardiovascularSystem.C01C_CardiacStimulantsExclCardiacGlycosides.C01CA03_Norepinephrine;
model Norepinephrine_Yoo2015_PD_se_drow
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Yoo_2015 :: SE_Drow (Subjective effects: Drowsiness)"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 9.5,      // [mm]
    Emax = -71.3,  // [mm]
    EC50 = 4.4e-06,  // [mol/m3; nmol/L × 1e-06]
    gamma = 4.2,
    exposure_per_s = 1e-06);   // 1 nmol/L per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 44, Interval = 0.088),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Norepinephrine_Yoo2015_PD_se_drow</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Yoo H et al., <i>European journal of clinical pharmacology 71(10):1197–1207</i> 2015 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00228-015-1913-0\">doi:10.1007/s00228-015-1913-0</a>) — Subjective effects: Drowsiness [mm] against norepinephrine nmol/L — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =        9.5 mm       drug-free response (baseline) (E0, Q324)
  Emax  =       71.3 mm       maximal effect term (Emax, Q323)
  EC50  =        4.4 nmol/L   exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC50, Q321)
  gamma =        4.2          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one nmol/L of norepinephrine per second of simulated time (exposure is in mol/m3): there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 9.5   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (4.4 nmol/L)  response -26.15
  exposure -> infinity  response -61.8</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Yoo_2015: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Norepinephrine_Yoo2015_PD_se_drow;
